17
00:04:15,680 --> 00:04:18,400
Goo Hyo Seon

18
00:04:21,180 --> 00:04:22,320
Hello?

19
00:04:22,320 --> 00:04:25,760
I just saw the magazine.

20
00:04:25,760 --> 00:04:26,710
Where is it?

21
00:04:26,710 --> 00:04:29,140
I'm saying I saw the magazine.

22
00:04:29,140 --> 00:04:33,050
The magazine that has Dad's face on it...

23
00:04:33,050 --> 00:04:34,880
Where are you?

24
00:04:34,880 --> 00:04:37,090
I'm on my way to Dong Soo's.

25
00:04:38,450 --> 00:04:39,830
You're going to Dong Soo's?

26
00:04:39,860 --> 00:04:42,520
Business K: The person who lives again through Dae Seong Saccaromycetes.

27
00:04:42,530 --> 00:04:44,760
Yes.

28
00:04:44,760 --> 00:04:48,390
There's a rice wine tasting competition later tonight.

29
00:04:48,390 --> 00:04:51,370
Dong Soo told me to come a bit early.

30
00:04:51,370 --> 00:04:55,240
Hello? Hello?

31
00:04:56,730 --> 00:04:58,750
Dong Soo

32
00:05:06,130 --> 00:05:09,580
Dong Soo, don't tell Hyo Seon anything!

33
00:05:09,580 --> 00:05:10,400
What do you mean?

34
00:05:10,400 --> 00:05:13,870
The things you told me earlier. Hyo Seon can't know that.

35
00:05:13,870 --> 00:05:15,380
Really?

36
00:05:20,120 --> 00:05:23,660
Okay. Aren't you coming?

37
00:05:23,660 --> 00:05:26,040
Hurry up. You need to come, too.

38
00:05:26,040 --> 00:05:29,910
I wonder. I don't think I'll be able to make it, Hyo Seon.

39
00:05:29,910 --> 00:05:32,650
Do you know what's going on here now?

40
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:37,520
The phones have started ringing off the hook now. Wait a moment.

41
00:05:41,230 --> 00:05:44,580
Thank you. This is Dae Seong True Winemakers.

42
00:05:44,580 --> 00:05:49,580
Of course you can order right now. How much do you need?

43
00:05:49,580 --> 00:05:51,540
Yes, yes I understand.

44
00:05:51,540 --> 00:05:53,980
Could you please email us your order form?

45
00:05:53,980 --> 00:05:56,390
Yes. Yes, thank you.

46
00:05:56,390 --> 00:05:58,720
Hello. Did you hear that?

47
00:05:58,720 --> 00:06:03,920
Yes. I heard it. That's a relief.

48
00:06:03,920 --> 00:06:08,040
But here too, I didn't just come to this tasting contest to play and have fun.

49
00:06:08,070 --> 00:06:10,880
I was hoping it would help us promote our wine.

50
00:06:10,900 --> 00:06:14,220
Think of it as work and I want you to make time to come.

51
00:06:15,190 --> 00:06:18,090
Hello, this is Dae Seong True Winemakers

52
00:06:29,500 --> 00:06:33,220
The person who lives again through Dae Seong Saccaromycetes.

53
00:06:40,150 --> 00:06:42,780
Hyo Seon can't know about it!

54
00:06:52,100 --> 00:06:55,330
Dae Seong True Winemakers

55
00:07:26,900 --> 00:07:30,260
Eun Jo. I'm okay, can you open up?

56
00:07:31,730 --> 00:07:34,130
Eun Jo. Are you okay?

57
00:07:34,130 --> 00:07:36,020
Open up.

58
00:07:59,970 --> 00:08:04,470
Hong Gi Hoon, who works at your company, is their youngest son.

59
00:08:04,470 --> 00:08:06,920
Did you know that?

60
00:08:32,530 --> 00:08:34,850
You're quick.

61
00:08:36,820 --> 00:08:40,430
I did think you'd come find me again,

62
00:08:40,430 --> 00:08:43,660
but this is sooner than I expected.

63
00:08:43,660 --> 00:08:46,190
How many brothers do you have?

64
00:08:48,290 --> 00:08:51,780
You have a younger brother, right?

65
00:08:56,080 --> 00:09:00,820
Did my younger brother wrong you?

66
00:09:02,760 --> 00:09:07,440
He practically lives his day to day with a picture of your sister, Goo Hyo Seon.

67
00:09:07,440 --> 00:09:11,560
Did he seek your home, by chance?

68
00:09:12,530 --> 00:09:15,970
He won't mature, despite his age.

69
00:09:15,970 --> 00:09:19,960
If he's made some kind of mistake, I'll apologize on his behalf.

70
00:09:21,320 --> 00:09:25,910
I'm not sure I understand what you mean.

71
00:09:25,910 --> 00:09:28,240
Didn't you ask about my younger brother?

72
00:09:28,240 --> 00:09:30,950
Yes, I did.

73
00:09:35,390 --> 00:09:39,000
What was your question?

74
00:09:42,350 --> 00:09:46,230
Do you have a younger brother named Hong Gi Hoon?

75
00:09:51,110 --> 00:09:53,040
So you do.

76
00:09:59,050 --> 00:10:00,700
I understand.

77
00:10:00,700 --> 00:10:02,730
Sit.

78
00:10:03,900 --> 00:10:09,030
I said sit. A conversation can't be one-sided.

79
00:10:17,390 --> 00:10:21,130
My younger brother's name is Hong Gi Tae.

80
00:10:21,130 --> 00:10:24,560
That guy named Hong Gi Hoon is not my brother.

81
00:10:26,380 --> 00:10:29,350
Although he's not my brother,

82
00:10:30,270 --> 00:10:33,320
he is indeed my father's son.

83
00:10:35,560 --> 00:10:42,580
It seems like you know something. You can ask for the details from Gi Hoon or my father.

84
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:45,980
I have nothing to tell you.

85
00:10:47,520 --> 00:10:49,410
So...

86
00:10:50,960 --> 00:10:54,410
all Hong Joo Ga's family members worked together,

87
00:10:55,690 --> 00:10:57,680
along with Hong Gi Hoon...

88
00:10:57,680 --> 00:10:59,380
Stop.

89
00:11:02,270 --> 00:11:05,420
This isn't something you should be saying to me.

90
00:11:06,320 --> 00:11:10,860
I didn't ask you to sit here for me to hear this.

91
00:11:13,080 --> 00:11:17,280
If you find out about the truth from Gi Hoon or my father,

92
00:11:17,280 --> 00:11:20,660
you'll definitely want to meet me again.

93
00:11:21,420 --> 00:11:27,260
That means I would want to cooperate with you to do absolutely anything.

94
00:11:28,780 --> 00:11:31,180
Let's talk again then.

95
00:11:34,140 --> 00:11:36,090
Excuse me.

96
00:11:37,840 --> 00:11:41,490
There has never been anyone who gets up before I do.

97
00:11:43,710 --> 00:11:45,370
Why not?

98
00:11:46,960 --> 00:11:50,000
There also hasn't been anyone who asks that.

99
00:12:31,300 --> 00:12:36,010
Eun Jo, now I really

100
00:12:36,610 --> 00:12:38,730
can't go ...

101
00:12:40,580 --> 00:12:41,570
to you...

102
00:12:41,570 --> 00:12:46,050
At least you can repay Ahjusshi like this.

103
00:12:47,330 --> 00:12:49,300
I don't have a way to repay him.

104
00:12:51,090 --> 00:12:55,830
I'm jealous you have a way.

105
00:12:57,770 --> 00:13:03,610
It's already too late. I can't.

106
00:13:03,610 --> 00:13:06,870
The person who lives again through Dae Seong Saccaromycetes.

107
00:14:17,500 --> 00:14:18,860
Take her home.

108
00:14:18,860 --> 00:14:21,960
Okay, I got it.

109
00:14:21,960 --> 00:14:25,680
What are you guys doing?

110
00:14:33,900 --> 00:14:35,710
So...

111
00:14:37,300 --> 00:14:40,880
you people colluded

112
00:14:40,880 --> 00:14:43,620
and killed someone.

113
00:14:46,500 --> 00:14:52,060
I thought I had done that...

114
00:14:53,760 --> 00:14:55,250
So ...

115
00:14:57,510 --> 00:15:00,280
I wasn't the only one...

116
00:15:02,080 --> 00:15:04,850
who was pushing down my dad.

117
00:15:06,390 --> 00:15:08,970
So many people against one person...

118
00:15:10,160 --> 00:15:12,080
And ...

119
00:15:13,500 --> 00:15:16,260
that person was part of it too, wasn't he?

120
00:15:17,380 --> 00:15:18,990
That person...

121
00:15:20,390 --> 00:15:23,260
colluded with you guys, didn't he?

122
00:15:24,920 --> 00:15:29,280
So many people against one person...

123
00:15:29,280 --> 00:15:30,850
This means ...

124
00:15:31,990 --> 00:15:33,880
so many people ...

125
00:15:35,050 --> 00:15:37,420
ganged up like that

126
00:15:38,470 --> 00:15:40,690
on one person.

127
00:15:46,280 --> 00:15:50,670
Hey, you're really pale.

128
00:15:50,670 --> 00:15:53,460
Are you okay?

129
00:15:53,460 --> 00:15:55,700
What are you going to do?

130
00:15:56,800 --> 00:16:01,950
You guys are in serious trouble.

131
00:16:05,700 --> 00:16:08,370
I'm not going to let this go.

132
00:16:09,870 --> 00:16:14,360
What are you going to do?

133
00:17:01,900 --> 00:17:04,000
Sit here.

134
00:17:15,830 --> 00:17:18,100
What do you want?

135
00:17:23,280 --> 00:17:25,940
I'm hungry.

136
00:17:25,940 --> 00:17:28,730
I didn't eat anything this morning.

137
00:17:32,330 --> 00:17:34,560
Has your fever gone down?

138
00:17:35,940 --> 00:17:40,900
Your cold hasn't gone away yet, right?

139
00:17:40,900 --> 00:17:42,900
I'm fine.

140
00:17:44,070 --> 00:17:46,450
What do you want?

141
00:17:48,330 --> 00:17:50,010
I just...

142
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:53,760
didn't want to eat alone.

143
00:17:53,760 --> 00:17:56,580
That's not like you.

144
00:17:57,540 --> 00:18:00,610
Whether you care for me or not,

145
00:18:00,610 --> 00:18:04,870
you're not someone who would call me because you don't want to eat alone.

146
00:18:06,270 --> 00:18:10,650
Did Mom perhaps say something to you?

147
00:18:12,720 --> 00:18:15,120
Mom?

148
00:18:15,120 --> 00:18:17,320
Never mind, if that's not it.

149
00:18:24,850 --> 00:18:27,100
How are you feeling inside?

150
00:18:28,780 --> 00:18:34,090
You said you're heartbroken. How are you feeling?

151
00:18:38,850 --> 00:18:41,660
Don't misunderstand me.

152
00:18:41,660 --> 00:18:45,620
Because you're broken hearted, I can't help that.

153
00:18:45,620 --> 00:18:48,280
That's not what I mean.

154
00:18:48,280 --> 00:18:50,430
Are you curious

155
00:18:51,790 --> 00:18:53,690
about what it's like?

156
00:18:55,500 --> 00:19:01,020
Yes, I am. I said I would care more about you, didn't I?

157
00:19:02,420 --> 00:19:07,440
You might not believe me, but as your sister,

158
00:19:07,440 --> 00:19:16,280
or as a friend you keep seeing a lot of these days,

159
00:19:16,280 --> 00:19:18,960
I have the right to ask, don't I?

160
00:19:18,960 --> 00:19:21,170
Are you really curious?

161
00:19:21,170 --> 00:19:22,890
Yes.

162
00:19:24,990 --> 00:19:27,040
I'm curious.

163
00:19:30,730 --> 00:19:32,810
It hurts.

164
00:19:34,890 --> 00:19:37,960
Officially getting rejected

165
00:19:42,070 --> 00:19:44,420
really hurts.

166
00:19:52,430 --> 00:19:57,910
What kind of person is he?

167
00:19:59,270 --> 00:20:01,660
What do you mean?

168
00:20:02,690 --> 00:20:09,130
You two were close like siblings much longer than I knew him.

169
00:20:12,090 --> 00:20:14,610
I'm just curious.

170
00:20:16,420 --> 00:20:21,750
How did he join our family?

171
00:20:24,780 --> 00:20:30,480
Dad brought him in one day.

172
00:20:33,020 --> 00:20:39,390
He is the son of Dad's friend. He didn't have money for tuition, so he came to work part-time.

173
00:20:41,090 --> 00:20:47,360
Do you still have feelings for him?

174
00:20:50,430 --> 00:20:52,740
What do you think?

175
00:20:55,360 --> 00:20:57,820
I'm asking because I don't know.

176
00:21:01,170 --> 00:21:02,800
Yes.

177
00:21:08,220 --> 00:21:15,300
Even if Oppa leaves...even if he goes to another woman...

178
00:21:17,120 --> 00:21:23,630
even if I become someone who has nothing to do with him...

179
00:21:30,430 --> 00:21:33,890
Thanks for being curious about me.

180
00:21:52,040 --> 00:21:56,880
But still, I think you and I should get our stories in sync at least.

181
00:22:01,970 --> 00:22:07,660
I don't know just how much the eldest daughter knew before coming to see me,

182
00:22:07,660 --> 00:22:10,770
but now she knows that you're our father's son,

183
00:22:10,770 --> 00:22:14,590
doesn't that mean she knows why you went working there?

184
00:22:15,650 --> 00:22:19,560
That girl seems to believe that you and I have been conspiring against them.

185
00:22:19,560 --> 00:22:25,080
Because she seems so confident, things like legal action or reporting to the newspaper,

186
00:22:25,080 --> 00:22:28,940
it seemed like she'd be the kind of brazen puppy to do those kinds of things.

187
00:22:30,040 --> 00:22:34,920
How was Eun Jo?

188
00:22:34,920 --> 00:22:39,530
How she was... What does that mean?

189
00:22:40,460 --> 00:22:41,990
Did she cry?

190
00:22:41,990 --> 00:22:43,920
I'm not sure.

191
00:22:43,920 --> 00:22:50,560
I can't remember if she cried or not but she was shaking like a leaf.

192
00:22:51,900 --> 00:22:57,980
At the very least to make sure that girl doesn't run around wild, you'll have to take care of her.

193
00:22:57,980 --> 00:23:02,980
If she does, won't that be difficult for you, me, or our father?

194
00:23:02,980 --> 00:23:07,660
She's not here yet.

195
00:23:08,890 --> 00:23:13,200
Where did she go, shaking like she was?

196
00:23:13,200 --> 00:23:18,690
Are you listening to what I'm saying or not? What nonsense are you spewing?

197
00:23:18,690 --> 00:23:21,370
Where did she go?!

198
00:23:22,610 --> 00:23:27,090
Did you just let that girl, who was shaking like that, go alone?

199
00:23:27,090 --> 00:23:30,420
Why didn't you call me before letting her leave like that?!

200
00:23:47,200 --> 00:23:49,320
He looks a little uncertain.

201
00:23:49,320 --> 00:23:52,370
The next person up is Miss Goo Hyo Seon. Applause.

202
00:24:12,190 --> 00:24:15,380
Oh my god, what's going on? What's wrong with her?

203
00:24:15,380 --> 00:24:18,320
- I don't think she's sure.
- How can Goo Hyo Seon not know?

204
00:24:18,320 --> 00:24:20,870
Shouldn't she know Dae Seong True Winemakers, her family's own wine?

205
00:24:20,910 --> 00:24:22,950
- She's not sure.
- What's wrong with her?

206
00:24:22,950 --> 00:24:24,960
Hyo Seon should know it, obviously.

207
00:24:25,000 --> 00:24:26,380
Why isn't she saying anything?

208
00:24:26,380 --> 00:24:28,860
- She can't seem to taste it.
Why can't she?

209
00:24:32,300 --> 00:24:35,850
Next person up will be Kim In Gyeong.

210
00:25:00,900 --> 00:25:04,280
Let's go. We need to talk.

211
00:25:04,280 --> 00:25:06,390
All right!

212
00:25:09,070 --> 00:25:11,100
That's all right!

213
00:25:14,790 --> 00:25:17,790
Next up is participant Lee Hyo Jae.

214
00:25:40,700 --> 00:25:42,000
Let's talk.

215
00:25:42,000 --> 00:25:44,890
About what? I have nothing to say to you.

216
00:25:44,890 --> 00:25:46,250
Let go.

217
00:25:46,250 --> 00:25:49,490
- I have something to say.
- No! I'm not going to listen.

218
00:25:49,490 --> 00:25:54,840
I tried to tell you before. I didn't want you to find out from someone else.

219
00:25:54,840 --> 00:25:57,950
Eun Jo. Eun Jo.

220
00:26:06,730 --> 00:26:10,390
Let go! Let go!

221
00:26:10,390 --> 00:26:12,600
I said to let go of me!

222
00:26:26,990 --> 00:26:30,170
Eun Jo. Eun Jo!

223
00:26:31,280 --> 00:26:34,300
- Eun Jo, wait -
- Let go. Let go, let go!

224
00:26:34,300 --> 00:26:36,180
Let go!

225
00:26:36,180 --> 00:26:37,930
I said let go.

226
00:26:37,930 --> 00:26:39,820
Let go...

227
00:26:43,450 --> 00:26:46,270
What excuses are you trying to make?

228
00:26:47,920 --> 00:26:50,960
I can't hear it yet.

229
00:26:50,960 --> 00:26:56,470
If I listen to you, I think my body will explode, shatter, and disappear!

230
00:26:58,460 --> 00:27:00,750
You bastard.

231
00:27:00,750 --> 00:27:06,040
You're the worst son of a b**ch in the world. You're the ground.

232
00:27:06,040 --> 00:27:08,560
Even from ground level, none could be worse.

233
00:27:08,560 --> 00:27:12,940
I don't even want to step on you! Disgusting!

234
00:27:14,360 --> 00:27:16,600
Listen to me now. Just listen right now.

235
00:27:16,600 --> 00:27:18,830
Let go! I don't want to!

236
00:27:18,830 --> 00:27:24,130
Right now. If a day passes, it'll be that much pain. If two days pass, it'll be two days worth of pain.

237
00:27:24,130 --> 00:27:26,560
I'll end it for you now. Let's end it here!

238
00:27:26,560 --> 00:27:28,290
Let go.

239
00:27:45,830 --> 00:27:51,280
Where did Oppa Gi Hoon and Unni Eun Jo go?

240
00:27:52,600 --> 00:27:55,500
They left for some work at the factory.

241
00:27:55,500 --> 00:27:59,680
Is it really for work at the factory?

242
00:27:59,680 --> 00:28:03,550
Yes. It's really for work at the factory.

243
00:28:03,550 --> 00:28:06,370
What work at the factory?

244
00:28:07,380 --> 00:28:10,250
I'm not sure about that either.

245
00:28:17,020 --> 00:28:21,760
What relationship do you and Eun Jo have?

246
00:28:25,290 --> 00:28:27,450
Did Eun Jo not tell you?

247
00:28:27,450 --> 00:28:32,960
She doesn't talk about that kind of stuff. You know how she is.

248
00:28:32,960 --> 00:28:36,120
When we were younger, we lived in the same house once.

249
00:28:37,770 --> 00:28:39,350
In the same house?

250
00:28:39,350 --> 00:28:41,540
Yes, in the same house.

251
00:28:41,540 --> 00:28:44,450
Before Noona came, there was no one who cooked for us...

252
00:28:44,450 --> 00:28:49,060
In the same house, even with my Mom?

253
00:28:49,060 --> 00:28:51,500
Yes.

254
00:28:51,500 --> 00:28:54,400
I don't think Mom knows you.

255
00:28:54,400 --> 00:28:57,630
Ajhumma was never interested in me.

256
00:28:57,630 --> 00:28:59,650
Of course she doesn't know me.

257
00:28:59,650 --> 00:29:01,850
Did Mom...

258
00:29:04,710 --> 00:29:07,490
live with your dad?

259
00:29:07,490 --> 00:29:12,990
No, he's not my father. He's just someone who raised me.

260
00:29:12,990 --> 00:29:16,790
Is his name...

261
00:29:18,100 --> 00:29:20,950
Jang Taek Geun?

262
00:29:24,490 --> 00:29:26,560
It's not.

263
00:29:28,170 --> 00:29:30,430
It's really not.

